# Build output. The installers are NOT tracked: they are release artifacts, and
# the GitHub release is the only place they are published.
#
# They used to be committed here, which meant every release added ~170 MB to
# history and, worse, put a second copy of each installer in the repository that
# was not the one anyone downloaded - Inno Setup does not produce identical bytes
# twice, so the CI-built release asset and the committed copy always differed.
# The repository's own .sha256 files therefore described a build that existed
# only on one machine.
#
# Get an installer from the release:
#   https://github.com/ACTstudent/RemoteAcessMonitoringSoftware4sale/releases/latest
# Or build one with .\build-everything.ps1, which recreates these folders.
server-dist/
client-dist/

# Test result files written by build-everything.ps1 and CI
test-results/
